# Page and Component Creation Patterns

When creating new pages or major UI components in the Mini App, **ALWAYS** follow these established patterns.

## Page Structure Pattern

### 1. File Organization
- Place pages in `miniapp/src/pages/` for routed pages
- Place feature components in `miniapp/src/` for embedded components (like `Commands.tsx`, `Broadcast.tsx`)
- Use PascalCase for component names

### 2. Component Signature Pattern

```tsx
// For feature components with props
interface ComponentProps {
  botId: string;
  view: "list" | "edit" | "other-views";
  onViewChange?: (view: string) => void;
  onCanSaveChange?: (canSave: boolean) => void;
  saveRef?: React.MutableRefObject<() => void>;
  // ... other props
}

export function ComponentName({ botId, view, onViewChange, ... }: ComponentProps) {
  // Implementation
}

// For page components
export const PageName: React.FC = () => {
  // Implementation
};
```

### 3. Standard Imports

```tsx
import React, { useEffect, useState, useCallback } from "react";
import { useNavigate, useParams } from "react-router-dom";
import { 
  Section, 
  ListItem, 
  ToggleItem, 
  FormField,
  FormTextAreaField,
  FormSelectField,
  Loader,
  Button,
  Page,
  // ... other components needed
} from "./components"; // or "../components" for pages
import { useTranslation } from "./i18n"; // or "../i18n"
import { useBots } from "./store/BotContext"; // or "../store/BotContext"
import { useBackButton } from "./hooks/useBackButton"; // if needed
import { useMainButton } from "./hooks/useMainButton"; // if needed
```

### 4. State Management Pattern

```tsx
export function ComponentName({ botId, ... }: Props) {
  const { t, translateError } = useTranslation();
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  
  // Loading states
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [saving, setSaving] = useState(false);
  
  // UI states
  const [status, setStatus] = useState<string>("");
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);
  
  // Data
  const [items, setItems] = useState<ItemType[]>([]);
  
  // Form state
  const [form, setForm] = useState({
    field1: "",
    field2: "",
    // ...
  });

  // ... rest of implementation
}
```

### 5. Data Loading Pattern

```tsx
const loadData = useCallback(async () => {
  try {
    setLoading(true);
    setError(null);
    const data = await fetchData(botId);
    setItems(data);
  } catch (e: any) {
    setError(translateError(e));
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
}, [botId, translateError]);

useEffect(() => {
  loadData();
}, [loadData]);
```

### 6. Loading State Rendering

```tsx
// ALWAYS use Loader component, never plain text
if (loading) {
  return <Loader text={t("miniapp.loading")} />;
}

// For pages with Page wrapper
if (loading && !data) {
  return <Page><Loader /></Page>;
}

// For fullscreen loading during operations
{saving && <Loader fullscreen text={status} />}
```

### 7. Form Section Pattern

**CRITICAL: By default, ALWAYS use Section with `title` prop for form fields:**

```tsx
// ✅ DEFAULT PATTERN: Section title + plain input (PREFERRED)
<Section title={t("miniapp.field_name")}>
  <FormInput
    placeholder={t("miniapp.field_placeholder")}
    value={form.fieldName}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, fieldName: e.target.value })}
  />
</Section>

<Section title={t("miniapp.description")}>
  <FormTextArea
    placeholder={t("miniapp.description_placeholder")}
    value={form.description}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, description: e.target.value })}
    rows={4}
  />
</Section>

<Section title={t("miniapp.category")} contentClassName="ui-section-padded">
  <CustomSelect
    value={form.category}
    onChange={(val) => setForm({ ...form, category: val })}
    options={[
      { value: "a", label: "Option A" },
      { value: "b", label: "Option B" },
    ]}
  />
</Section>

// ❌ BAD: Using FormField/FormTextAreaField/FormSelectField (only use when absolutely necessary)
<Section>
  <FormField label="Name" ... />
</Section>

// ⚠️ ALTERNATIVE: Only use FormField when you need inline label + hint in same section
<Section>
  <FormField
    label={t("miniapp.field_name")}
    hint={t("miniapp.field_hint")}
    placeholder={t("miniapp.field_placeholder")}
    value={form.fieldName}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, fieldName: e.target.value })}
  />
</Section>

// ✅ GOOD: Group related fields in one section
<Section title={t("miniapp.user_info")}>
  <FormInput placeholder={t("miniapp.name")} hasDivider ... />
  <FormInput placeholder={t("miniapp.email")} ... />
</Section>
```

**Key Rules:**
1. ✅ **DEFAULT**: Use `<Section title="...">` + `<FormInput>` / `<FormTextArea>` / `<CustomSelect>`
2. ✅ Each field in its own Section for visual separation
3. ⚠️ Only use `FormField` / `FormTextAreaField` / `FormSelectField` when you need label + hint inside the section
4. ❌ Never put multiple unrelated fields in one continuous Section

### 8. Form Input Patterns

**Pattern 1: Section Title (DEFAULT - ALWAYS USE THIS):**

```tsx
// ✅ PREFERRED: Section title acts as label
<Section title={t("miniapp.field_name")}>
  <FormInput
    placeholder={t("miniapp.placeholder")}
    value={form.fieldName}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, fieldName: e.target.value })}
  />
</Section>

<Section title={t("miniapp.description")}>
  <FormTextArea
    placeholder={t("miniapp.placeholder")}
    value={form.description}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, description: e.target.value })}
    rows={4}
  />
</Section>

<Section title={t("miniapp.category")} contentClassName="ui-section-padded">
  <CustomSelect
    value={form.category}
    onChange={(val) => setForm({ ...form, category: val })}
    options={options}
  />
</Section>
```

**Note:** Use `contentClassName="ui-section-padded"` for sections containing `CustomSelect` or other elements that don't have built-in padding.

**Pattern 2: Composable Components with Internal Labels (USE SPARINGLY):**

```tsx
// ⚠️ Only use when you need label + hint together
<Section>
  <FormField
    label={t("miniapp.field_name")}
    hint={t("miniapp.field_hint")}
    placeholder={t("miniapp.placeholder")}
    value={form.fieldName}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, fieldName: e.target.value })}
  />
</Section>

<Section>
  <FormTextAreaField
    label={t("miniapp.description")}
    hint={t("miniapp.description_hint")}
    value={form.description}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, description: e.target.value })}
    rows={4}
  />
</Section>

<Section>
  <FormSelectField
    label={t("miniapp.category")}
    value={form.category}
    onChange={(val) => setForm({ ...form, category: val })}
    options={options}
  />
</Section>
```

**Pattern 3: Multiple Related Fields (Group in Section with Title):**

```tsx
// ✅ For grouped inputs like in Commands
<Section title={t("miniapp.command_info")}>
  <FormInput
    placeholder={t("miniapp.command")}
    value={form.command}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, command: e.target.value })}
    hasDivider
  />
  <FormInput
    placeholder={t("miniapp.description")}
    value={form.description}
    onChange={(e) => setForm({ ...form, description: e.target.value })}
  />
</Section>
```

### 9. Toggle Pattern

```tsx
<Section>
  <ToggleItem
    label={t("miniapp.toggle_label")}
    subtitle={t("miniapp.toggle_description")}
    checked={form.enabled}
    onChange={(val) => setForm({ ...form, enabled: val })}
